      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Every two minutes, somewhere in the world, a woman dies simply because she is a woman. These are not inevitable deaths; they are largely preventable. On June 9, 2025, Aga Khan University (AKU) Nairobi took a significant step in confronting this crisis by hosting the launch of the WomenXCollective. This vital event, held in conjunction with the AKU Centre of Excellence for Women and Child Health, the United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA) Kenya, Africa Centres for Disease Control (CDC) and Prevention, and the Government of Kenya, marked AKU's official inclusion in this global initiative. The launch underscored a united commitment to dismantle the silence that perpetuates these tragedies."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Growing up in Canada, the concept of violence against women felt distant, understood mainly through headlines. However, learning about femicide - the deliberate killing of women because of their gender - and the alarming statistics surrounding preventable maternal deaths dramatically shifted my perspective. Annually, over 80,000 women are killed by partners or family members, alongside countless others who die from treatable complications during childbirth. These numbers are a stark reminder of the urgent need for action."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "AKU President Sulaiman Shahabuddin perfectly articulated the collective's unwavering goal: \"We believe that the number of mothers who lose their lives due to preventable causes - the number of women whose family planning needs go unmet; and the number of girls and women who experience gender-based violence and harm - should all be zero.\" Not reduced, not improved - but zero. This bold vision highlights the profound commitment of the WomenXCollective."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The WomenXCollective is not merely an academic endeavor; it's a solutions-driven movement. By bringing evidence-based solutions to sexual and reproductive health, the initiative directly addresses communities most in need. With 165,000 deliveries at AKDN facilities in 2024 alone, AKU's tangible impact in saving lives is clear and continually expanding. AKU joined this powerful collective due to its shared values, the immense power of partnerships, and its unique expertise in healthcare and research."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Joining this movement means more than just acknowledging a crisis; it means becoming an active part of the solution. Participants gain access to the latest research, connect with advocates globally, and develop practical skills that can be applied anywhere. Ultimately, it's about joining an essential cause to create a world where every woman lives without fear, survives childbirth, and thrives knowing her life is valued."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "To learn more and become part of this vital movement, visit our website at"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "https://www.aku.edu/coe-wch/ea/Pages/home-1.aspx",
